{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PUvfkQDqMRnY6Xy58ucraJ","type":"tool_result","content":"128	- `FND-0166` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'hypotheses': ['(CE)', '(N)', '(BAL)', 'S is reduced and locally Noetherian', 'the genus-six family is proper and smooth over S', 'h^0(L_s)=3 for every geometric fibre', 'L is fibrewise base-point-free', 'projectivizations use the line convention', 'the representation-theoretic assertion uses Q-coefficients and a Q-linear cohomological theory having transfer for free finite étale quotients'], 'mathematical_scope': 'The promoted result identifies the incidence divisor as a projective bundle and identifies the S_5-invariants of transfer-compatible rational cohomology with the multiplicity spaces for [6] and [5,1]. It does not establish Tate type, control other S_6-isotypics, or apply integrally or to functors lacking finite-quotient transfer.', 'objects': ['script-C', 'L', 'A', 'script-D', 'script-G', 'U', 'Z^(1)', 'Z'], 'subproblem_id': 'C66-TATE-SUPPORT'}]: Let S be a reduced locally Noetherian scheme carrying a proper smooth genus-six degree-four family satisfying (CE), (N), and (BAL), with associated fibre-degree-six line bundle L such that h^0(C_s,L_s)=3 for every geometric fibre s and L_s is base-point-free. Let pi:script-C→S be the family, let A be its relative linear system of one-dimensional spaces of sections of L, and let script-D be the universal degree-six divisor in script-C x_S A. Write Delta_script-C for the diagonal in script-C x_S script-C and pr_1,pr_2 for its projections. Then script-G:=pr_{2*}(pr_1^*L(-Delta_script-C)) is locally free of rank two on script-C and is compatible with arbitrary base change. Using the line convention for projectivization, the incidence morphism (p,Gamma)↦p identifies script-D canonically with P_script-C(script-G), hence with a Zariski-locally trivial P^1-bundle over script-C. Let U⊂A be the reduced-support locus, let Z→U be the finite étale right S_6-torsor of orderings, and put Z^(1):=script-D x_A U. Then Z^(1) is open in script-D, is finite étale of degree six over U, and is canonically Z/S_5 for the stabilizer S_5 of the first letter. If F is a Q-linear cohomological theory with transfer for free finite étale quotients, then F(Z^(1))≅F(Z)^{S_5}≅Hom_{S_6}(Ind_{S_5}^{S_6}(1),F(Z))≅M_[6](F(Z)) direct-sum M_[5,1](F(Z)), because Ind_{S_5}^{S_6}(1)≅[6] direct-sum [5,1]. Thus Z^(1) recovers the multiplicity spaces of the [6] and [5,1] isotypic summands; it is not itself their direct sum as S_6-subrepresentations. This applies, where defined, to rational ordinary, compactly supported, or Borel–Moore cohomology and their mixed Hodge structures and weight-graded pieces. It asserts neither Tate type nor control of other S_6-isotypics and does not extend to integral coefficients or functors without finite-quotient transfer.
129	- `FND-0167` [corroborated; {'base_field': 'C', 'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'conditional_content': ['Tate type for the [6] and [5,1] isotypic components requires (H-C)', 'Tate type for the S_6-invariant component requires (H-S)'], 'excluded': ['S_6-isotypic components other than [6] and [5,1]', 'Any top-weight vanishing with nonconstant coefficient systems', 'Tate-ness of the balanced tetragonal base or universal curve without (H-S) or (H-C)', 'Any morphism, Gysin map, support-exhaustion statement, or conclusion about M_{6,6}'], 'objects': ['T_16(Z)', 'Gr^W_16 H^16_c(Z;Q)', 'S_6-invariant multiplicity space', '[6] and [5,1] multiplicity Hodge structures'], 'subproblem_id': 'C66-TATE-SUPPORT', 'unconditional_content': ['Corner injections obtained from compact-support localization and projective-bundle formulas with constant Tate coefficients', 'Reduction of the trivial and standard multiplicity Hodge structures to constant-coefficient corners of the universal curve']}]: Work over C with Q-coefficients. Let S be a reduced separated finite-type C-scheme carrying the balanced genus-six degree-four setup needed below: a smooth proper genus-six curve pi: script-C -> S and a relative degree-six line bundle L such that h^0(script-C_s,L_s)=3 for every geometric s, formation of pi_*L commutes with base change, and every L_s is base-point-free. Put A=P_S(pi_*L), let script-D be the universal degree-six divisor in script-C times_S A, let Delta be the non-reduced-divisor locus, put U=A minus Delta, and let Z=Ord(U)->U be the finite etale right S_6-torsor of orderings. Assume, as proved in the originating setup from these balanced hypotheses, that A->S is a Zariski-locally trivial P^2-bundle, script-D->script-C is a Zariski-locally trivial P^1-bundle, and Z^(1):=script-D restricted to U equals Z/S_5 for the stabilizer S_5 of one letter. Define T_m(X)=W_{-m}H_m^{BM}(X;Q), canonically dual to Gr^W_m H_c^m(X;Q). Then compact-support localization and the projective-bundle formula give injections of pure polarizable weight-sixteen Hodge structures Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q)^{S_6}=Gr^W_16 H_c^16(U;Q) into Gr^W_16 H_c^16(S;Q) direct-sum Gr^W_14 H_c^14(S;Q)(-1) direct-sum Gr^W_12 H_c^12(S;Q)(-2), and Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q)^{S_5}=Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z^(1);Q) into Gr^W_16 H_c^16(script-C;Q) direct-sum Gr^W_14 H_c^14(script-C;Q)(-1). All coefficient objects in these ambient projective-bundle formulas are constant Tate objects, so the nonconstant-coefficient obstruction FND-0164 does not apply. More precisely, if Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q)=direct-sum_rho V_rho tensor M_rho is its rational S_6-isotypic decomposition, then Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q)^{S_5} is isomorphic as a Hodge structure to M_[6] direct-sum M_[5,1], not to the full isotypic subrepresentation. Under (H-C), namely Gr^W_16 H_c^16(script-C;Q) is a finite direct sum of Q(-8) and Gr^W_14 H_c^14(script-C;Q) is a finite direct sum of Q(-7), semisimplicity implies that M_[6] and M_[5,1] are direct sums of Q(-8); consequently the full [6] and [5,1] isotypic components of T_16(Z), after duality, are direct sums of Q(8). Under (H-S), namely Gr^W_{2j}H_c^{2j}(S;Q) is a finite direct sum of Q(-j) for j=6,7,8, the S_6-invariant part of T_16(Z), equivalently T_16(U), is a direct sum of Q(8). Duality reverses the displayed compact-support injections into Borel-Moore surjections. No assertion is made about other S_6-isotypics, the truth of (H-C) or (H-S), nonconstant coefficient systems, or M_{6,6}.
130	- `FND-0168` [corroborated; {'ambient': 'smooth proper Deligne-Mumford stack Mbar_{6,6} of dimension 21 with boundary D = Mbar_{6,6} minus M_{6,6}, D proper', 'base_field': 'C', 'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'does_not_assert': ['that K fails to be Tate of type Q(-8)', 'that the Z-supported contribution fails to be Tate', 'that Z-supported classes do not in fact span K', 'any computation of H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) or of the RED-0001 target', 'any claim outside (g,n)=(6,6), although the logical structure of clauses (2)-(4) is general', 'any refutation of ATT-0116 clause (a) or of CL-01 through CL-04, which the audit confirms'], 'hypotheses': ['M_{6,6} smooth, so H^k_c(M_{6,6};Q) has weights <= k', 'D proper, so H^{15}(D;Q) has weights <= 15', 'morphisms of mixed Hodge structures are strict, so Gr^W_k is exact', 'Q-coefficients throughout; stack-level Betti cohomology, no integral or coarse-space content', "for clause (3), a closed support in M_{6,6} must be fixed before the phrase 'contribution supported on Z' has a referent"], 'objects': ['K = ker(H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) -> H^{16}(D;Q))', 'Gr^W_{16}H^{16}_c(M_{6,6};Q)', 'RED-0001 open input W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q)', 'balanced Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure locus Z and any closure of its image in M_{6,6}', 'ATT-0116 theorem clause (b) and claim CL-05'], 'subproblem_id': 'C66-TATE-SUPPORT'}]: Scope: (g,n)=(6,6) over C with Q-coefficients; Mbar_{6,6} the smooth proper Deligne-Mumford stack of dimension d=21, D = Mbar_{6,6} minus M_{6,6} its proper boundary, Z the balanced Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure locus. (1) K := ker(H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) -> H^{16}(D;Q)) is canonically isomorphic, as a pure polarizable Hodge structure of weight 16, to Gr^W_{16}H^{16}_c(M_{6,6};Q) -- the top weight graded piece of H^{16}_c and the entire degree-16 compact-support corner of M_{6,6} -- and is canonically the Hodge-structure dual of the RED-0001 open input W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q), with Q(-8) dual to Q(8). This uses only smoothness of M_{6,6} (weights of H^{16}_c are <= 16), properness of D (weights of H^{15}(D) are <= 15) and strictness. It is a global invariant of M_{6,6} and carries no support condition. The separate Poincare identification W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q) = W_{26}H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q)(21) (FND-0001) is a different map and must not be conflated with this duality. (2) For any pure Q-Hodge structure V of weight 16, 'V is a finite direct sum of Q(-8)' and 'V is spanned by its Hodge (8,8)-classes' are the same condition (V_C = V^{8,8}) by the definition of Hodge type; neither polarizability nor semisimplicity of the category of pure polarizable weight-16 Q-Hodge structures is needed for this equivalence, and neither adds information to it. Applied to K, the equivalence is a restatement of the target, not a reduction: it imposes no support condition and produces no cycle class. (Semisimplicity, per FND-0033, only excludes extension gaps at this corner.) (3) Give 'the contribution supported on Z' its only standard meaning by first fixing a closed support Y in M_{6,6} containing the image of Z. Since Gr^W is exact on mixed Hodge structures, the Borel-Moore localization sequence yields an exact sequence W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(Y;Q) -> W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q) -> W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6} minus Y;Q). Consequently: (3a) if the Z-supported contribution means the image of the first map, then K Tate of type Q(-8) implies that contribution is Tate (a sub-object of a type-(8,8) structure is of type (8,8)), so Z-Tate is necessary; but the converse -- the direction the reduction needs -- does not follow, since it additionally requires a support-exhaustion input, namely vanishing or Tate-ness of the quotient injecting into W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16} of the complement of Y. No such input is established for (6,6). (3b) if it means W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(Y;Q) itself, then neither direction follows, since only the image of that group is constrained by K. ATT-0116 fixes neither reading. Hence the asserted equivalence 'the contribution supported on Z is Tate of the exact target type if and only if K is spanned by Hodge (8,8)-classes' is unproved and is a non-sequitur in its load-bearing direction. This is a statement about a missing hypothesis, not a demonstration that the two sides have different truth values: if the RED-0001 target is Tate, both sides hold, so the biconditional cannot be refuted by exhibiting differing truth values. (4) 'K is spanned by algebraic fundamental classes of codimension-8 cycles of Mbar_{6,6} supported on a closure of Z' implies 'K is spanned by Hodge (8,8)-classes', but the converse is the Hodge conjecture in codimension 8 on the 21-dimensional Mbar_{6,6}, which is unproved in general beyond the (1,1) case; writing 'equivalently' between the two silently assumes it. (5) Independently of (3) and (4), the support clause carries two further undischarged obligations: (5a) a closed (stratified) embedding of the balanced reduced-support model into M_{6,6}/Mbar_{6,6} together with a Gysin map -- that model is an open piece of the failure locus (FND-0052), and FND-0147 supplies only a representable unramified quasi-finite monomorphism to M_{6,6}, which is not a closed immersion of a pure-codimension-4 closed substack; (5b) the Gysin degree shift H^{8}(Z-tilde;Q)(-4) -> H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) for a 17-dimensional codimension-4 support with a suitable smooth model Z-tilde. The phrase 'codimension-8 cycles supported on the closure of Z' is itself degree-consistent (codimension 8 in Mbar_{6,6} equals codimension 4 on the 17-dimensional support), so the defect is the unwritten shift and the missing closed embedding, not the codimension label; the fundamental class of the support itself lies in H^{8}, not H^{16}. Not asserted: that K fails to be Tate; that the Z-supported contribution fails to be Tate; that Z-supported classes do not in fact span K; any computation of H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q); any claim for (g,n) other than (6,6), although the logical structure of (2)-(4) is general. Confirmed and untouched: ATT-0116 clause (a) and claims CL-01 through CL-04.
131	- `FND-0169` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'excluded': ['Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q) for Z=Ord(U)', 'stack-level compactly supported cohomology of Hbar^bal', 'the global kernel K', 'RED-0001', 'nonconstant coefficient objects'], 'ground_field': 'C', 'j': 8, 'objects': ['reduced separated finite-type C-scheme bases carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family', 'etale scheme atlases of Hbar^bal', 'Gr^W_16 H_c^16', 'hypothesis (H-S) of FND-0167']}]: Over C with Q-coefficients, at (g,n)=(6,6). Let Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2] be the smooth Deligne-Mumford stack of pure dimension 15 of balanced genus-six degree-four covers (FND-0162). Let S range over reduced separated finite-type C-schemes carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family in the sense of FND-0167, including connected components of reduced separated finite-type etale scheme atlases of Hbar^bal. The constant-coefficient corner Gr^W_16 H_c^16(S;Q) is not an invariant of the stack Hbar^bal: it depends on S. Explicitly, the mu_3-Kummer cover C->M_{0,4} cut out by y^3=x(x-1), with smooth projective model Cbar of genus one, yields a nonempty irreducible finite-etale cover Mtilde of M_{0,18} whose Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Mtilde;Q) contains a nonzero Hodge type (15,1), obtained as the compact-support Kunneth summand Q(-1) tensor H^{1,0}(Cbar)^{tensor 14} and surviving removal of the pairwise-diagonal locus of dimension at most 14 because Hodge numbers of compactly supported cohomology vanish in filtration degree strictly larger than dimension (Deligne, Theorie de Hodge III, Theorem 8.2.4(ii)). By the Bujokas-Patel theorem that the Casnati-Ekedahl bundle F of a general cover in the classical simply-branched Hurwitz space H_{d,g} is balanced whenever g>=(d-3)(d-1) (hence for (d,g)=(4,6)), together with FND-0159 (the classical Hurwitz space is etale over the configuration space of r=2g+2d-2=18 points), there is a connected finite-etale Hurwitz chart X over M_{0,18} whose balanced open is nonempty. Finite-etale pullback/trace of 