134	- `FND-0172` [corroborated; {'applies_to': 'any construction that needs a simply-branched balanced cover, including any Hurwitz chart etale over M_{0,18} or Conf_18', 'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'cover': {'F': 'O(4)+O(5)', 'degree': 4, 'genus': 6}, 'does_not_assert': ['Tate-ness of Z=Ord(U) or of RED-0001', 'irreducibility or the number of connected components of H^bal', 'closedness of the composed or type-(ii) locus', 'that CLM-0112-4 is the unique existence route'], 'ground_field': 'algebraically closed of characteristic zero', 'objects': ['H=H_{4,6}(P^1)', 'H^bal', 'Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2]', 'simply-branched locus', 'classical Hurwitz space H_{4,6}']}]: Let k be an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero. Let H=H_{4,6}(P^1) be the Deligne-Mumford stack of finite degree-four covers of a fixed P^1 by smooth connected genus-six curves, and let H^bal be the open locus where the Casnati-Ekedahl relations bundle in the packet orientation F=ker(Sym^2 E -> gamma_*(omega_{C/P^1}^{otimes 2})) is isomorphic to O_{P^1}(4)+O_{P^1}(5) (rank two, degree +9). Write Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2]. Call gamma simply branched when every geometric fibre has partition type 2+1+1+1, equivalently when every local monodromy permutation in S_4 is a transposition, equivalently when gamma has eighteen distinct simple branch values. (1) The packet's self-contained nonemptiness witness for H^bal (FND-0154: gamma=q o psi through a smooth genus-one curve) is never simply branched. This is FND-0158: a nontrivial factorization C->Y->P^1 of degrees (2,2) has a fibre of type (2,2) or 4 over each branch value of q, since every degree-two map Y->P^1 is ramified (Riemann-Hurwitz: deg R_q=2g_Y+2>=2); equivalently, a simply-branched connected degree-four cover has monodromy group S_4, which is primitive, while a nontrivial factorization is imprimitive. Under the extra reducedness and disjointness hypotheses of FND-0158(b), the FND-0154 family has fourteen branch values (ten of type 2+1+1 and four of