never 2j>2 dim Delta_0. Thus the fibre-degree-2 summand Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q)(-2) always survives in such product families as a direct Kunneth summand of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q), equivalently H_c^4(U_0;Q)=Q(-2), because H_c^4 of a curve vanishes; this is the class used by ATT-0119. If Delta_0 is nonempty and proper then H_c^0(U_0;Q)=0, so the fibre-degree-0 summand Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S;Q) does not appear in H_c^{16}(U;Q); the restriction H_c^2(P^2)->H_c^2(Delta_0) is typically nonzero for a positive-degree plane curve, so the fibre-degree-1 projective-bundle summand need not arise from U. Independently, on a non-product FND-0167 family with S of pure dimension 15, the discriminant Delta subset A has dimension 16, so Deligne's Hodge-number bound (Theorie de Hodge III, Theorem 8.2.4(ii)) does not force F^{15} H_c^{16}(Delta;C)=0. This is why FND-0171 blocks transporting the (H-S) j=8 / fibre-degree-0 first summand of ATT-0118 to U, while it does not block the ATT-0119 fibre-fundamental-class class, which is already a Kunneth summand of H_c^{16}(U) itself. The FND-0167 corner map injects Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U) into the three summands and cannot by itself transport non-Tateness from any ambient summand to U; survival of the third summand in product families is a kernel/Kunneth statement, not a reverse of that injection. Fibrewise restriction on Delta_0 does not by itself control non-product families at fibre degrees j=0,1 without a compact-support Leray argument, which FND-0164 withholds for nonconstant coefficients. No assertion is made about RED-0001, about T_16 of a dimension-17 model over a dimension-15 atlas of Hbar^bal, or about S_6-isotypics other than the S_6-invariants of the product model.
137	- `FND-0178` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'does_not_assert': ['failure of RED-0001', 'failure of T_16 on a named 15-dimensional etale atlas of Hbar^bal', 'failure of the FND-0167 implication under (H-S) or (H-C)', 'any closed embedding, Gysin map, image, or support-exhaustion statement in M_{6,6}'], 'ground_field': 'C', 'surviving_class': 'nonzero Hodge type (10,6) in Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q), S_6-invariant, from the Kunneth summand Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S) tensor H_c^4(U_0)=Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S)(-2)', 'theorem_disproved': 'TASK-C66-M-004/C66-TATE-SUPPORT as universally quantified over every reduced locally Noetherian C-scheme carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) genus-six degree-four family with no connected-component image contained in the type-(ii) locus, with no dimension, dominance, or non-isotriviality hypothesis', 'witness_base': 'S=C_aff^8, C_aff the affine Kummer curve of y^3=x(x-1) minus the three ramification points of x, equipped with the constant simply-branched balanced type-(i) family', 'witness_dimensions': {'S': 8, 'U': 10, 'Z': 10}}]: Work over C with Q-coefficients. Let C_aff be the smooth connected affine curve obtained from the smooth projective model Cbar of y^3=x(x-1) by deleting the three ramification points of the degree-three x-map: Cbar has genus one by Riemann-Hurwitz, H_c^2(C_aff;Q)=Q(-1) of type (1,1), and Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C_aff;Q) is isomorphic to H^1(Cbar;Q) of types (1,0) and (0,1). Let S=C_aff^8, a smooth connected affine C-scheme of dimension 8, in particular reduced, locally Noetherian, separated, and of finite type. Compact-support Kunneth of mixed Hodge structures places a nonzero Hodge type-(8,4) class in Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q), arising from the summand Q(-1)^{tensor 4} tensor (Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C_aff;Q))^{tensor 4}. Let (C_0,gamma_0) be a simply-branched balanced type-(i) geometric fibre of H^bal (existence by FND-0172, equivalently Bujokas-Patel: the Casnati-Ekedahl bundle of a general cover in H_{d,g} is balanced for g>=(d-3)(d-1), hence at (d,g)=(4,6)). The constant (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family over S with this fibre is an allowed ATT-0112 clause-(E) base: its classifying image is a single type-(i) point, hence not contained in the type-(ii) locus. For this family, U isomorphic to S times U_0 and Z isomorphic to S times Z_0, where U_0 is the reduced-support open in |L_0| isomorphic to P^2, a smooth connected surface, so H_c^4(U_0;Q)=Q(-2) of type (2,2). Compact-support Kunneth therefore realises Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q)(-2) as a direct mixed-Hodge-structure summand of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q), carrying a nonzero Hodge type-(10,6) class (permitted by Deligne's Hodge-number bound on the 10-fold U). Finite-etale transfer over Q injects this S_6-invariant class into Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q). A finite direct sum of Q(-8) is pure of type (8,8), so Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q) is not a finite direct sum of Q(-8) and T_16(Z):=W_{-16} H^{BM}_{16}(Z;Q), dual with no extra Tate twist, is not a finite direct sum of Q(8). Consequently the exact TASK-C66-M-004/C66-TATE-SUPPORT theorem, as universally quantified over every reduced locally Noetherian C-scheme carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) genus-six degree-four family with no connected-component image contained in the type-(ii) locus and with no dimension, dominance, or non-isotriviality hypothesis, is false. The witness lies entirely in the simply-branched locus and already in the S_6-invariant ([6]) isotypic component. The class is a Kunneth summand of H_c^{16}(U) itself, namely the third FND-0167 corner Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S)(-2), not a lift of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S), so FND-0171 does not block it. This does not resolve RED-0001, does not address T_16 of a dimension-17 model over a named 15-dimensional etale atlas of Hbar^bal, and does not refute the conditional implication of FND-0167, because the witness base violates (H-S) at j=6 and at j=7 (while the j=8 instance of (H-S) holds for this particular S)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2feb1a14-4beb-4569-bd03-58f265d02787","uuid":"1a481544-29df-484b-8534-e3903d8c94a5","timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:33:25.816Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/r_/40tyr0nj6zn_yqb74rw_351c0000gn/T/pure-tate-agent-toj0r0qb/proof/packets/generated/C66-001-v5.md","content":"- `FND-0166` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'hypotheses': ['(CE)', '(N)', '(BAL)', 'S is reduced and locally Noetherian', 'the genus-six family is proper and smooth over S', 'h^0(L_s)=3 for every geometric fibre', 'L is fibrewise base-point-free', 'projectivizations use the line convention', 'the representation-theoretic assertion uses Q-coefficients and a Q-linear cohomological theory having transfer for free finite étale quotients'], 'mathematical_scope': 'The promoted result identifies the incidence divisor as a projective bundle and identifies the S_5-invariants of transfer-compatible rational cohomology with the multiplicity spaces for [6] and [5,1]. It does not establish Tate type, control other S_6-isotypics, or apply integrally or to functors lacking finite-quotient transfer.', 'objects': ['script-C', 'L', 'A', 'script-D', 'script-G', 'U', 'Z^(1)', 'Z'], 'subproblem_id': 'C66-TATE-SUPPORT'}]: Let S be a reduced locally Noetherian scheme carrying a proper smooth genus-six degree-four family satisfying (CE), (N), and (BAL), with associated fibre-degree-six line bundle L such that h^0(C_s,L_s)=3 for every geometric fibre s and L_s is base-point-free. Let pi:script-C→S be the family, let A be its relative linear system of one-dimensional spaces of sections of L, and let script-D be the universal degree-six divisor in script-C x_S A. Write Delta_script-C for the diagonal in script-C x_S script-C and pr_1,pr_2 for its projections. Then script-G:=pr_{2*}(pr_1^*L(-Delta_script-C)) is locally free of rank two on script-C and is compatible with arbitrary base change. Using the line convention for projectivization, the incidence morphism (p,Gamma)↦p identifies script-D canonically with P_script-C(script-G), hence with a Zariski-locally trivial P^1-bundle over script-C. Let U⊂A be the reduced-support locus, let Z→U be the finite étale right S_6-torsor of orderings, and put Z^(1):=script-D x_A U. Then Z^(1) is open in script-D, is finite étale of degree six over U, and is canonically Z/S_5 for the stabilizer S_5 of the first letter. If F is a Q-linear cohomological theory with transfer for free finite étale quotients, then F(Z^(1))≅F(Z)^{S_5}≅Hom_{S_6}(Ind_{S_5}^{S_6}(1),F(Z))≅M_[6](F(Z)) direct-sum M_[5,1](F(Z)), because Ind_{S_5}^{S_6}(1)≅[6] direct-sum [5,1]. Thus Z^(1) recovers the multiplicity spaces of the [6] and [5,1] isotypic summands; it is not itself their direct sum as S_6-subrepresentations. This applies, where defined, to rational ordinary, compactly supported, or Borel–Moore cohomology and their mixed Hodge structures and weight-graded pieces. It asserts neither Tate type nor control of other S_6-isotypics and does not extend to integral coefficients or functors without finite-quotient transfer.
- `FND-0167` [corroborated; {'base_field': 'C', 'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'conditional_content': ['Tate type for the [6] and [5,1] isotypic components requires (H-C)', 'Tate type for the S_6-invariant component requires (H-S)'], 'excluded': ['S_6-isotypic components other than [6] and [5,1]', 'Any top-weight vanishing with nonconstant coefficient systems', 'Tate-ness of the balanced tetragonal base or universal curve without (H-S) or (H-C)', 'Any morphism, Gysin map, support-exhaustion statement, or conclusion about M_{6,6}'], 'objects': ['T_16(Z)', 'Gr^W_16 H^16_c(Z;Q)', 'S_6-invariant multiplicity space', '[6] and [5,1] multiplicity Hodge structures'], 'subproblem_id': 'C66-TATE-SUPPORT', 'unconditional_content': ['Corner injections obtained from compact-support localization and projective-bundle formulas with constant Tate coefficients', 'Reduction of the trivial and standard multiplicity Hodge structures to constant-coefficient corners of the universal curve']}]: Work over C with Q-coefficients. Let S be a reduced separated finite-type C-scheme carrying the balanced genus-six degree-four setup needed below: a smooth proper genus-six curve pi: script-C -> S and a relative degree-six line bundle L such that h^0(script-C_s,L_s)=3 for every geometric s, formation of pi_*L commutes with base change, and every L_s is base-point-free. Put A=P_S(pi_*L), let script-D be the universal degree-six divisor in script-C times_S A, let Delta be the non-reduced-divisor locus, put U=A minus Delta, and let Z=Ord(U)->U be the finite etale right S_6-torsor of orderings. Assume, as proved in the originating setup from these balanced hypotheses, that A->S is a Zariski-locally trivial P^2-bundle, script-D->script-C is a Zariski-locally trivial P^1-bundle, and Z^(1):=script-D restricted to U equals Z/S_5 for the stabilizer S_5 of one letter. Define T_m(X)=W_{-m}H_m^{BM}(X;Q), canonically dual to Gr^W_m H_c^m(X;Q). Then compact-support localization and the projective-bundle formula give injections of pure polarizable weight-sixteen Hodge structures Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q)^{S_6}=Gr^W_16 H_c^16(U;Q) into Gr^W_16 H_c^16(S;Q) direct-sum Gr^W_14 H_c^14(S;Q)(-1) direct-sum Gr^W_12 H_c^12(S;Q)(-2), and Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q)^{S_5}=Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z^(1);Q) into Gr^W_16 H_c^16(script-C;Q) direct-sum Gr^W_14 H_c^14(script-C;Q)(-1). All coefficient objects in these ambient projective-bundle formulas are constant Tate objects, so the nonconstant-coefficient obstruction FND-0164 does not apply. More precisely, if Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q)=direct-sum_rho V_rho tensor M_rho is its rational S_6-isotypic decomposition, then Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q)^{S_5} is isomorphic as a Hodge structure to M_[6] direct-sum M_[5,1], not to the full isotypic subrepresentation. Under (H-C), namely Gr^W_16 H_c^16(script-C;Q) is a finite direct sum of Q(-8) and Gr^W_14 H_c^14(script-C;Q) is a finite direct sum of Q(-7), semisimplicity implies that M_[6] and M_[5,1] are direct sums of Q(-8); consequently the full [6] and [5,1] isotypic components of T_16(Z), after duality, are direct sums of Q(8). Under (H-S), namely Gr^W_{2j}H_c^{2j}(S;Q) is a finite direct sum of Q(-j) for j=6,7,8, the S_6-invariant part of T_16(Z), equivalently T_16(U), is a direct sum of Q(8). Duality reverses the displayed compact-support injections into Borel-Moore surjections. No assertion is made about other S_6-isotypics, the truth of (H-C) or (H-S), nonconstant coefficient systems, or M_{6,6}.
- `FND-0168` [corroborated; {'ambient': 'smooth proper Deligne-Mumford stack Mbar_{6,6} of dimension 21 with boundary D = Mbar_{6,6} minus M_{6,6}, D proper', 'base_field': 'C', 'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'does_not_assert': ['that K fails to be Tate of type Q(-8)', 'that the Z-supported contribution fails to be Tate', 'that Z-supported classes do not in fact span K', 'any computation of H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) or of the RED-0001 target', 'any claim outside (g,n)=(6,6), although the logical structure of clauses (2)-(4) is general', 'any refutation of ATT-0116 clause (a) or of CL-01 through CL-04, which the audit confirms'], 'hypotheses': ['M_{6,6} smooth, so H^k_c(M_{6,6};Q) has weights <= k', 'D proper, so H^{15}(D;Q) has weights <= 15', 'morphisms of mixed Hodge structures are strict, so Gr^W_k is exact', 'Q-coefficients throughout; stack-level Betti cohomology, no integral or coarse-space content', "for clause (3), a closed support in M_{6,6} must be fixed before the phrase 'contribution supported on Z' has a referent"], 'objects': ['K = ker(H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) -> H^{16}(D;Q))', 'Gr^W_{16}H^{16}_c(M_{6,6};Q)', 'RED-0001 open input W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q)', 'balanced Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure locus Z and any closure of its image in M_{6,6}', 'ATT-0116 theorem clause (b) and claim CL-05'], 'subproblem_id': 'C66-TATE-SUPPORT'}]: Scope: (g,n)=(6,6) over C with Q-coefficients; Mbar_{6,6} the smooth proper Deligne-Mumford stack of dimension d=21, D = Mbar_{6,6} minus M_{6,6} its proper boundary, Z the balanced Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure locus. (1) K := ker(H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) -> H^{16}(D;Q)) is canonically isomorphic, as a pure polarizable Hodge structure of weight 16, to Gr^W_{16}H^{16}_c(M_{6,6};Q) -- the top weight graded piece of H^{16}_c and the entire degree-16 compact-support corner of M_{6,6} -- and is canonically the Hodge-structure dual of the RED-0001 open input W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q), with Q(-8) dual to Q(8). This uses only smoothness of M_{6,6} (weights of H^{16}_c are <= 16), properness of D (weights of H^{15}(D) are <= 15) and strictness. It is a global invariant of M_{6,6} and carries no support condition. The separate Poincare identification W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q) = W_{26}H^{26}(M_{6,6};Q)(21) (FND-0001) is a different map and must not be conflated with this duality. (2) For any pure Q-Hodge structure V of weight 16, 'V is a finite direct sum of Q(-8)' and 'V is spanned by its Hodge (8,8)-classes' are the same condition (V_C = V^{8,8}) by the definition of Hodge type; neither polarizability nor semisimplicity of the category of pure polarizable weight-16 Q-Hodge structures is needed for this equivalence, and neither adds information to it. Applied to K, the equivalence is a restatement of the target, not a reduction: it imposes no support condition and produces no cycle class. (Semisimplicity, per FND-0033, only excludes extension gaps at this corner.) (3) Give 'the contribution supported on Z' its only standard meaning by first fixing a closed support Y in M_{6,6} containing the image of Z. Since Gr^W is exact on mixed Hodge structures, the Borel-Moore localization sequence yields an exact sequence W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(Y;Q) -> W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6};Q) -> W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(M_{6,6} minus Y;Q). Consequently: (3a) if the Z-supported contribution means the image of the first map, then K Tate of type Q(-8) implies that contribution is Tate (a sub-object of a type-(8,8) structure is of type (8,8)), so Z-Tate is necessary; but the converse -- the direction the reduction needs -- does not follow, since it additionally requires a support-exhaustion input, namely vanishing or Tate-ness of the quotient injecting into W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16} of the complement of Y. No such input is established for (6,6). (3b) if it means W_{-16}H^{BM}_{16}(Y;Q) itself, then neither direction follows, since only the image of that group is constrained by K. ATT-0116 fixes neither reading. Hence the asserted equivalence 'the contribution supported on Z is Tate of the exact target type if and only if K is spanned by Hodge (8,8)-classes' is unproved and is a non-sequitur in its load-bearing direction. This is a statement about a missing hypothesis, not a demonstration that the two sides have different truth values: if the RED-0001 target is Tate, both sides hold, so the biconditional cannot be refuted by exhibiting differing truth values. (4) 'K is spanned by algebraic fundamental classes of codimension-8 cycles of Mbar_{6,6} supported on a closure of Z' implies 'K is spanned by Hodge (8,8)-classes', but the converse is the Hodge conjecture in codimension 8 on the 21-dimensional Mbar_{6,6}, which is unproved in general beyond the (1,1) case; writing 'equivalently' between the two silently assumes it. (5) Independently of (3) and (4), the support clause carries two further undischarged obligations: (5a) a closed (stratified) embedding of the balanced reduced-support model into M_{6,6}/Mbar_{6,6} together with a Gysin map -- that model is an open piece of the failure locus (FND-0052), and FND-0147 supplies only a representable unramified quasi-finite monomorphism to M_{6,6}, which is not a closed immersion of a pure-codimension-4 closed substack; (5b) the Gysin degree shift H^{8}(Z-tilde;Q)(-4) -> H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q) for a 17-dimensional codimension-4 support with a suitable smooth model Z-tilde. The phrase 'codimension-8 cycles supported on the closure of Z' is itself degree-consistent (codimension 8 in Mbar_{6,6} equals codimension 4 on the 17-dimensional support), so the defect is the unwritten shift and the missing closed embedding, not the codimension label; the fundamental class of the support itself lies in H^{8}, not H^{16}. Not asserted: that K fails to be Tate; that the Z-supported contribution fails to be Tate; that Z-supported classes do not in fact span K; any computation of H^{16}(Mbar_{6,6};Q); any claim for (g,n) other than (6,6), although the logical structure of (2)-(4) is general. Confirmed and untouched: ATT-0116 clause (a) and claims CL-01 through CL-04.
- `FND-0169` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'excluded': ['Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q) for Z=Ord(U)', 'stack-level compactly supported cohomology of Hbar^bal', 'the global kernel K', 'RED-0001', 'nonconstant coefficient objects'], 'ground_field': 'C', 'j': 8, 'objects': ['reduced separated finite-type C-scheme bases carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family', 'etale scheme atlases of Hbar^bal', 'Gr^W_16 H_c^16', 'hypothesis (H-S) of FND-0167']}]: Over C with Q-coefficients, at (g,n)=(6,6). Let Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2] be the smooth Deligne-Mumford stack of pure dimension 15 of balanced genus-six degree-four covers (FND-0162). Let S range over reduced separated finite-type C-schemes carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family in the sense of FND-0167, including connected components of reduced separated finite-type etale scheme atlases of Hbar^bal. The constant-coefficient corner Gr^W_16 H_c^16(S;Q) is not an invariant of the stack Hbar^bal: it depends on S. Explicitly, the mu_3-Kummer cover C->M_{0,4} cut out by y^3=x(x-1), with smooth projective model Cbar of genus one, yields a nonempty irreducible finite-etale cover Mtilde of M_{0,18} whose Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Mtilde;Q) contains a nonzero Hodge type (15,1), obtained as the compact-support Kunneth summand Q(-1) tensor H^{1,0}(Cbar)^{tensor 14} and surviving removal of the pairwise-diagonal locus of dimension at most 14 because Hodge numbers of compactly supported cohomology vanish in filtration degree strictly larger than dimension (Deligne, Theorie de Hodge III, Theorem 8.2.4(ii)). By the Bujokas-Patel theorem that the Casnati-Ekedahl bundle F of a general cover in the classical simply-branched Hurwitz space H_{d,g} is balanced whenever g>=(d-3)(d-1) (hence for (d,g)=(4,6)), together with FND-0159 (the classical Hurwitz space is etale over the configuration space of r=2g+2d-2=18 points), there is a connected finite-etale Hurwitz chart X over M_{0,18} whose balanced open is nonempty. Finite-etale pullback/trace of the type-(15,1) class along a connected component Xtilde of X times_{M_{0,18}} Mtilde, followed by compact-support localization onto the balanced open V of Xtilde (FND-0165), produces a connected smooth 15-fold V, etale over Hbar^bal, with Gr^{15,1} Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(V;C) nonzero. Thus Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(V;Q) is not a finite direct sum of Q(-8). For any allowed atlas U, the disjoint union U sqcup V is again an allowed atlas and compactly supported cohomology is additive, so the same non-Tate summand appears in Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U sqcup V;Q). Consequently the j=8 instance of hypothesis (H-S) of FND-0167, namely that Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S;Q) is a finite direct sum of Q(-8), is false for some allowed S. FND-0167 itself does not assert (H-S). Any campaign statement that asserts or requires (H-S) while universally quantifying over a reduced locally Noetherian scheme atlas of Hbar^bal, or over all reduced separated finite-type C-schemes carrying the balanced setup, is therefore false as stated rather than merely unproved. (H-S) may be asserted only for a specifically named atlas, or replaced by a stack-level statement, which requires a compact-support mixed-Hodge formalism for Deligne-Mumford stacks that FND-0165 explicitly withholds. This does not address Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q) for Z=Ord(U): the FND-0167 corner map injects Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U) into a sum of Tate twists of corners of S, so it cannot transport non-Tateness from S to Z, and the discriminant in the Abel-Jacobi P^2-bundle has dimension 16 so F^{15} H_c^{16} need not vanish there.
- `FND-0170` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'dimension': 'd>=2', 'excludes': ['merely dominant morphisms that are neither finite etale nor open immersions', 'compactly supported mixed Hodge theory of Deligne-Mumford stacks without a scheme atlas', 'non-Tateness of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q) for the Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure model', 'RED-0001'], 'ground_field': 'C', 'includes': 'every simply-branched Hurwitz chart whose branch map is finite etale over M_{0,r} with r=d+3', 'objects': ['smooth connected complex algebraic d-fold W', 'finite etale morphism W->M_{0,d+3} or dense open immersion W->M_{0,d+3}', "connected component W' of the base change of the product mu_3-Kummer cover"], 'subproblem_id': 'C66-TATE-SUPPORT'}]: Work over C with Q-coefficients. Let d≥2 be an integer. Let B=M_{0,4}≅P^1 minus {0,1,∞}. Let Cbar be the smooth projective connected curve with function field C(x,y) and equation y^3=x(x-1): the degree-three map Cbar→P^1 given by x is totally ramified over exactly 0,1,∞ (valuations of x(x-1) equal 1,1,−2, none divisible by 3), and Riemann-Hurwitz gives 2g(Cbar)−2=3(−2)+3(2)=0, so Cbar has genus one. Let C be Cbar minus those three ramification points, so C→B is connected finite etale of degree three. Compact-support localization yields Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C;Q)≅H^1(Cbar;Q) of Hodge types (1,0) and (0,1), and H_c^2(C;Q)≅Q(−1); also H_c^0(C)=0. Identifying M_{0,d+3} with the complement of the pairwise diagonals in B^d, set Mtilde:=C^d ×_{B^d} M_{0,d+3}. This is a nonempty Zariski-open in the irreducible d-fold C^d, hence irreducible, and Mtilde→M_{0,d+3} is connected finite etale. Compact-support Kunneth of mixed Hodge structures places, for each of the d choices of factor, a direct summand Q(−1)⊗(Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C;Q))^{⊗(d−1)} inside Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(C^d;Q); the Hodge component (1,1)+(d−1)·(1,0)=(d,1) is one-dimensional and nonzero. The inverse image Y of the pairwise diagonals has dimension ≤d−1, so the Hodge numbers of H_c^{d+1}(Y) vanish for p>dim Y and therefore F^d H_c^{d+1}(Y;C)=0. Morphisms of mixed Hodge structures are strict for W and F; weights of H_c^d(Y;Q) are at most d; hence Gr^W_{d+1} of the compact-support localization sequence H_c^{d+1}(Mtilde)→H_c^{d+1}(C^d)→H_c^{d+1}(Y) is exact (FND-0165), the type-(d,1) class dies in H_c^{d+1}(Y), and it lifts to a nonzero class of Hodge type (d,1) in Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(Mtilde;Q). In particular F^d Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(Mtilde;C)≠0. For d≥2 one has d>(d+1)/2, so this weight-equals-degree corner is non-Tate. Now let W be a smooth connected complex algebraic d-fold equipped with a finite etale morphism f:W→M_{0,d+3}, and let W' be any connected component of W×_{M_{0,d+3}} Mtilde. Then W'→W is finite etale of positive degree, W'→Mtilde is finite etale of positive degree, and finite-etale pullback/trace over Q injects the type-(d,1) class into Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(W';Q). The same non-Tate class is obtained if instead f is a dense open immersion, by a second application of FND-0165 to the complement of dimension ≤d−1. Consequently the property that Gr^W_{d+1} H_c^{d+1}(−;Q) is Tate is not invariant under finite etale refinement of any such base, and no Tate assertion for that corner can be proved by an argument that is invariant under finite etale pullback, transfer, averaging, monodromy-orbit counting, or descent along an etale scheme atlas. This applies in particular to every simply-branched Hurwitz chart whose branch map is finite etale over M_{0,r} with r=d+3. The statement does not apply to a merely dominant morphism that is neither finite etale nor an open immersion; it does not assert anything about compactly supported cohomology of a Deligne-Mumford stack in the absence of a scheme atlas; and it does not transport non-Tateness to Gr^W_{16} H_c^{16}(Z;Q) of a Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure model, nor to RED-0001.
- `FND-0171` [corroborated; {'coefficients': 'Q', 'dimensions': {'A': 17, 'Delta': 16, 'S': 15}, 'g': 6, 'ground_field': 'C', 'hypotheses': ['S a reduced separated finite-type C-scheme of pure dimension 15 carrying (CE)+(N)+(BAL)', 'L fibrewise base-point-free with h^0=3, formation of pi_*L commuting with base change, so A=P_S(pi_*L) is a Zariski-locally trivial P^2-bundle', 'U=A minus Delta is the reduced-support open', 'Z=Ord(U)->U is the finite etale right S_6-torsor of orderings'], 'n': 6, 'objects': ['Gr^W_16 H_c^16(S;Q)', 'Gr^W_16 H_c^16(U;Q)', 'Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q)', 'Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q)^{S_6}', 'T_16(Z)'], 'setup': 'FND-0167 balanced Casnati-Ekedahl evaluation-failure model Z=Ord(U)'}]: Work over C with Q-coefficients in the FND-0167 setup for (g,n)=(6,6). Let S be a reduced separated finite-type C-scheme of pure dimension 15 carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) genus-six degree-four family whose relative degree-six line bundle L is fibrewise base-point-free with h^0=3, so that formation of pi_*L commutes with base change. Put A=P_S(pi_*L), a Zariski-locally trivial P^2-bundle of dimension 17; let Delta be the non-reduced-divisor locus; put U=A minus Delta; and let Z=Ord(U)->U be the finite etale right S_6-torsor of orderings. FND-0167 supplies an injection of pure polarizable weight-16 Hodge structures Gr^W_16 H_c^16(Z;Q)^{S_6}=Gr^W_16 H_c^16(U;Q) into Gr^W_16 H_c^16(S;Q) direct-sum Gr^W_14 H_c^14(S;Q)(-1) direct-sum Gr^W_12 H_c^12(S;Q)(-2), obtained by composing the FND-0165 corner injection for the open immersion U subset A with the projective-bundle formula for A->S. Polarizable pure Q-Hodge structures of a fixed weight form a semisimple abelian category, so this injection propagates Tate type of Q(-8) from the three constant-coefficient S-corners (H-S) down to U and to the S_6-invariants of T_16(Z). It cannot propagate non-Tate type from S to U or to Z: a non-Tate ambient Hodge structure may contain a Tate subobject, and FND-0167 does not assert surjectivity of the corner map. Independently, fibrewise Bertini (the general member of |L| consists of six distinct points) together with the classical discriminant and dual-curve description of a spanned g^2_6 in |L| isomorphic to P^2 imply that Delta->S is nonempty of pure relative dimension one, hence dim Delta=16. Deligne's Hodge-number bound (h^{p,q}=0 for p greater than the dimension) therefore does not force F^{15} H_c^{16}(Delta;C)=0, so the type-(15,1) lifting argument used by ATT-0118, which requires the removed locus to have dimension at most 14, does not lift classes from A to U. Consequently ATT-0118's refutation of (H-S) at j=8 on an allowed atlas component does not refute Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q) or Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q), both of which remain open. A repair of C66-TATE-SUPPORT that treats the Z-clause as refuted by base-corner non-Tateness is invalid. The universally quantified base and universal-curve conjunct should be dropped or replaced by a named-atlas hypothesis; even on a named atlas, FND-0167 controls only Z^{S_6} via (H-S) and the [6] and [5,1] multiplicity spaces via (H-C), not the remaining S_6-isotypics.
- `FND-0172` [corroborated; {'applies_to': 'any construction that needs a simply-branched balanced cover, including any Hurwitz chart etale over M_{0,18} or Conf_18', 'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'cover': {'F': 'O(4)+O(5)', 'degree': 4, 'genus': 6}, 'does_not_assert': ['Tate-ness of Z=Ord(U) or of RED-0001', 'irreducibility or the number of connected components of H^bal', 'closedness of the composed or type-(ii) locus', 'that CLM-0112-4 is the unique existence route'], 'ground_field': 'algebraically closed of characteristic zero', 'objects': ['H=H_{4,6}(P^1)', 'H^bal', 'Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2]', 'simply-branched locus', 'classical Hurwitz space H_{4,6}']}]: Let k be an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero. Let H=H_{4,6}(P^1) be the Deligne-Mumford stack of finite degree-four covers of a fixed P^1 by smooth connected genus-six curves, and let H^bal be the open locus where the Casnati-Ekedahl relations bundle in the packet orientation F=ker(Sym^2 E -> gamma_*(omega_{C/P^1}^{otimes 2})) is isomorphic to O_{P^1}(4)+O_{P^1}(5) (rank two, degree +9). Write Hbar^bal=[H^bal/PGL_2]. Call gamma simply branched when every geometric fibre has partition type 2+1+1+1, equivalently when every local monodromy permutation in S_4 is a transposition, equivalently when gamma has eighteen distinct simple branch values. (1) The packet's self-contained nonemptiness witness for H^bal (FND-0154: gamma=q o psi through a smooth genus-one curve) is never simply branched. This is FND-0158: a nontrivial factorization C->Y->P^1 of degrees (2,2) has a fibre of type (2,2) or 4 over each branch value of q, since every degree-two map Y->P^1 is ramified (Riemann-Hurwitz: deg R_q=2g_Y+2>=2); equivalently, a simply-branched connected degree-four cover has monodromy group S_4, which is primitive, while a nontrivial factorization is imprimitive. Under the extra reducedness and disjointness hypotheses of FND-0158(b), the FND-0154 family has fourteen branch values (ten of type 2+1+1 and four of type (2,2)), and the set of simply-branched type-(ii) points is empty. Consequently FND-0154 may not be cited as a simply-branched balanced cover. (2) Existence of a simply-branched point of H^bal, equivalently of Hbar^bal, is not supplied by FND-0154, nor by the type-(i) density statement of FND-0162 (type (i) means not FND-0153 type (ii), which excludes only the bielliptic-through-a-plane-cubic case and still permits primitive non-simple ramification). Any construction that needs a simply-branched balanced cover — in particular any argument that places a Hurwitz chart etale over M_{0,18} or Conf_18 inside the balanced locus — must discharge existence by one of the following routes. Route A (packet-internal dimension comparison): H is smooth of pure dimension 18 at every point, independently of ramification profile (FND-0159). The classical Hurwitz space of a fixed ramification profile with r distinct branch values is etale over the configuration space of those r points and has dimension r, which equals 18 if and only if the cover is simply branched (FND-0159; Kanev, arXiv:math/0509154, Introduction: the discriminant map of the simply-branched Hurwitz space is etale onto Y^{(n)}-Delta, with Delta the codimension-one locus of non-simple divisors). Hence the non-simply-branched locus in H has dimension at most 17. Combined with nonemptiness of H^bal (FND-0154) and the fact that H^bal is open of pure dimension 18 (FND-0162, FND-0163), every nonempty connected component of H^bal, and of the quotient Hbar^bal of pure dimension 15, meets the simply-branched locus. Equivalently, after the PGL_2 quotient, the same comparison is the dual-confirmed bound dim(non-simply-branched)<=14 in Hbar^bal of pure dimension 15 recorded as CLM-0112-4. Route B (Bujokas-Patel genericity): for a general point of the classical irreducible simply-branched Hurwitz space H_{d,g}, the Casnati-Ekedahl bundle of quadrics F is balanced whenever g>=(d-3)(d-1) (Bujokas-Patel, arXiv:1504.03756v1, IMRN 2021, Main Theorem; algebraically closed field of characteristic zero). Here F is defined by 0->F->Sym^2 E->alpha_*(omega_alpha^{otimes 2})->0, with rk F=d(d-3)/2 and deg F=(d-3)(g+d-1), and balanced means h^1(End F)=0. At (d,g)=(4,6) one has g=6>=3, rk F=2, deg F=9, hence F isomorphic to O(4)+O(5), matching the packet orientation. This route does not use FND-0154. FND-0163 records it only inside a NOT ASSERTED clause, so a proof that invokes it must cite the theorem independently. (3) This existence hinge is inherited by every argument that realises an etale chart of Hbar^bal over M_{0,18} or Conf_18. It does not by itself control Gr^W_16 H_c^{16} of the evaluation-failure model Z, nor the campaign target RED-0001.
- `FND-0176` [corroborated; {'bases': 'reduced separated finite-type C-schemes B carrying the constant type-(i) family; the C^8 witness lies inside the reduced locally Noetherian quantification of ATT-0112 clause (E)', 'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'counterexample': 'B=C^8 for C the affine Kummer curve of FND-0170; U isomorphic to C^8 times U_0 of dimension 10; surviving Hodge type (10,6) in Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q) and in the S_6-invariants of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q)', 'excluded': ['RED-0001', 'the global kernel K (FND-0168)', 'stack-level compactly supported cohomology of Hbar^bal', 'transport of the j=8 first FND-0167 summand on a pure-dimension-15 atlas (FND-0171)'], 'ground_field': 'C', 'hypotheses': ['Q-coefficients over C', '(C_0,gamma_0) a geometric type-(i) fibre of H^bal, e.g. a simply-branched balanced fibre (FND-0172)', 'B reduced, separated, and of finite type over C', 'constant (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family', 'compact-support Kunneth of mixed Hodge structures', 'finite-etale S_6-transfer over Q'], 'objects': ['U isomorphic to B times U_0', 'Z=Ord(U)', 'Gr^W_m H_c^m(B;Q)(-2)', 'Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q)', 'T_16(Z)'], 'subproblem_id': 'C66-TATE-SUPPORT'}]: Work over C with Q-coefficients, at (g,n)=(6,6). Let (C_0,gamma_0) be a geometric type-(i) fibre of H^bal in the sense of FND-0153, for instance any simply-branched balanced fibre (existence: FND-0172). Let B be a reduced separated finite-type C-scheme. The constant (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family over B with fibre (C_0,gamma_0) is an allowed ATT-0112 clause-(E) base, because its classifying image is a single type-(i) point. For this family, A=P_B(pi_*L) is isomorphic to B times |L_0| isomorphic to B times P^2, the reduced-support open U_0 of |L_0| is a nonempty smooth connected affine surface (the complement of the discriminant curve of the spanned g^2_6), U is isomorphic to B times U_0, and Z=Ord(U) isomorphic to B times Z_0 is the finite etale right S_6-torsor of orderings. Poincare duality on the smooth connected surface U_0, equivalently compact-support localization of U_0 subset P^2 against the discriminant curve Delta_0 of dimension 1, yields H_c^4(U_0;Q) isomorphic to Q(-2), pure of type (2,2). Compact-support Kunneth of mixed Hodge structures for products of separated finite-type C-schemes (the compact-support form of Deligne, Theorie de Hodge III, Proposition 8.2.10) therefore realises H_c^m(B;Q)(-2) as a direct mixed-Hodge-structure summand of H_c^{m+4}(U;Q) for every integer m, and, Q(-2) being pure of weight 4 with Gr^W exact, realises Gr^W_m H_c^m(B;Q)(-2) as a direct summand of Gr^W_{m+4} H_c^{m+4}(U;Q). Finite-etale transfer over Q identifies Gr^W_{m+4} H_c^{m+4}(U;Q) with the S_6-invariants inside Gr^W_{m+4} H_c^{m+4}(Z;Q). Consequently any theorem asserting that Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q) is a finite direct sum of Q(-8) for every allowed clause-(E) base forces Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(B;Q) to be a finite direct sum of Q(-6) for every reduced separated finite-type C-scheme B. This last assertion is false: if C is the affine Kummer curve of FND-0170 (the smooth projective model of y^3=x(x-1) minus the three ramification points of x), then for B=C^8 compact-support Kunneth supplies a nonzero Hodge component of type (8,4) in Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(B;Q), namely Q(-1)^{tensor 4} tensor (Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C;Q))^{tensor 4} with the type-(1,0) line of H^1(Cbar) in each of the four H_c^1 factors, and tensoring with Q(-2) produces a nonzero type-(10,6) class in Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q) and hence in Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q). Type (10,6) satisfies Deligne's Hodge-number bound (Theorie de Hodge III, Theorem 8.2.4(ii)) for dim U=10 and is not of type (8,8), so Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q) is not a finite direct sum of Q(-8) and T_16(Z) is not a finite direct sum of Q(8). The exact C66-TATE-SUPPORT theorem of campaign revision 4, universally quantified over every reduced locally Noetherian C-scheme carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family with no connected-component image contained in the type-(ii) locus, is therefore false. A repaired C66-TATE-SUPPORT must either name a specific base or atlas, or retain the FND-0167 hypotheses (H-S) including the j=6 corner Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q). The exhibited class is the third FND-0167 summand Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S)(-2), realised as a Kunneth summand of H_c^{16}(U) itself on a product family, not a lift of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S); FND-0171, which blocks transport of the j=8 first summand through the corner injection on a pure-dimension-15 atlas, does not apply. Not asserted: any computation of the global kernel K, any conclusion about a fixed 15-dimensional atlas of Hbar^bal, or any statement about RED-0001.
- `FND-0177` [corroborated; {'H_S_index_disambiguation': 'fibre degree 2j for j=0,1,2 versus (H-S) j=8 for the first summand', 'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'excluded': ['transport of non-Tateness by the FND-0167 injection itself', 'compact-support Leray with nonconstant coefficients on non-product families (FND-0164)', 'RED-0001', 'T_16 of a dimension-17 model over a dimension-15 atlas of Hbar^bal', 'S_6-isotypics other than S_6-invariants of the product model'], 'fibre_degrees': [0, 1, 2], 'ground_field': 'C', 'hypotheses': ['S reduced separated finite-type over C', 'Delta_0 closed in P^2 of dimension at most 1', 'constant or product (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family so A is the trivial P^2-bundle', 'Q-coefficients and mixed Hodge structures'], 'objects': ['Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q)', 'Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S;Q)', 'Gr^W_14 H_c^{14}(S;Q)(-1)', 'Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q)(-2)', 'product families U=S x U_0 with U_0=P^2 minus Delta_0']}]: Work over C with Q-coefficients. Let S be a reduced separated finite-type C-scheme, let Delta_0 subset P^2 be a closed subscheme of dimension at most 1, and set U_0=P^2 minus Delta_0. For a product (equivalently, constant (CE)+(N)+(BAL)) family with U isomorphic to S times U_0, compact-support Kunneth of mixed Hodge structures and the projective-bundle formula identify Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S times P^2;Q) with the direct sum of three pure weight-16 summands Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S;Q) direct-sum Gr^W_14 H_c^{14}(S;Q)(-1) direct-sum Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q)(-2), corresponding to fibre degrees 2j for j=0,1,2. Compact-support localization along U_0 subset P^2 is a long exact sequence of mixed Hodge structures; at the weight-equals-degree corner Gr^W is exact, so the fibre-degree-2j projective-bundle summand of A=S times P^2 lies in the image of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q) if and only if the restriction Gr^W_{2j} H_c^{2j}(P^2;Q) -> Gr^W_{2j} H_c^{2j}(Delta_0;Q) vanishes. Vanishing of H_c^{2j}(Delta_0;Q) is sufficient for that restriction to vanish, and holds whenever 2j>2 dim Delta_0. Thus the fibre-degree-2 summand Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q)(-2) always survives in such product families as a direct Kunneth summand of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q), equivalently H_c^4(U_0;Q)=Q(-2), because H_c^4 of a curve vanishes; this is the class used by ATT-0119. If Delta_0 is nonempty and proper then H_c^0(U_0;Q)=0, so the fibre-degree-0 summand Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S;Q) does not appear in H_c^{16}(U;Q); the restriction H_c^2(P^2)->H_c^2(Delta_0) is typically nonzero for a positive-degree plane curve, so the fibre-degree-1 projective-bundle summand need not arise from U. Independently, on a non-product FND-0167 family with S of pure dimension 15, the discriminant Delta subset A has dimension 16, so Deligne's Hodge-number bound (Theorie de Hodge III, Theorem 8.2.4(ii)) does not force F^{15} H_c^{16}(Delta;C)=0. This is why FND-0171 blocks transporting the (H-S) j=8 / fibre-degree-0 first summand of ATT-0118 to U, while it does not block the ATT-0119 fibre-fundamental-class class, which is already a Kunneth summand of H_c^{16}(U) itself. The FND-0167 corner map injects Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U) into the three summands and cannot by itself transport non-Tateness from any ambient summand to U; survival of the third summand in product families is a kernel/Kunneth statement, not a reverse of that injection. Fibrewise restriction on Delta_0 does not by itself control non-product families at fibre degrees j=0,1 without a compact-support Leray argument, which FND-0164 withholds for nonconstant coefficients. No assertion is made about RED-0001, about T_16 of a dimension-17 model over a dimension-15 atlas of Hbar^bal, or about S_6-isotypics other than the S_6-invariants of the product model.
- `FND-0178` [corroborated; {'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'does_not_assert': ['failure of RED-0001', 'failure of T_16 on a named 15-dimensional etale atlas of Hbar^bal', 'failure of the FND-0167 implication under (H-S) or (H-C)', 'any closed embedding, Gysin map, image, or support-exhaustion statement in M_{6,6}'], 'ground_field': 'C', 'surviving_class': 'nonzero Hodge type (10,6) in Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q), S_6-invariant, from the Kunneth summand Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S) tensor H_c^4(U_0)=Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S)(-2)', 'theorem_disproved': 'TASK-C66-M-004/C66-TATE-SUPPORT as universally quantified over every reduced locally Noetherian C-scheme carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) genus-six degree-four family with no connected-component image contained in the type-(ii) locus, with no dimension, dominance, or non-isotriviality hypothesis', 'witness_base': 'S=C_aff^8, C_aff the affine Kummer curve of y^3=x(x-1) minus the three ramification points of x, equipped with the constant simply-branched balanced type-(i) family', 'witness_dimensions': {'S': 8, 'U': 10, 'Z': 10}}]: Work over C with Q-coefficients. Let C_aff be the smooth connected affine curve obtained from the smooth projective model Cbar of y^3=x(x-1) by deleting the three ramification points of the degree-three x-map: Cbar has genus one by Riemann-Hurwitz, H_c^2(C_aff;Q)=Q(-1) of type (1,1), and Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C_aff;Q) is isomorphic to H^1(Cbar;Q) of types (1,0) and (0,1). Let S=C_aff^8, a smooth connected affine C-scheme of dimension 8, in particular reduced, locally Noetherian, separated, and of finite type. Compact-support Kunneth of mixed Hodge structures places a nonzero Hodge type-(8,4) class in Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q), arising from the summand Q(-1)^{tensor 4} tensor (Gr^W_1 H_c^1(C_aff;Q))^{tensor 4}. Let (C_0,gamma_0) be a simply-branched balanced type-(i) geometric fibre of H^bal (existence by FND-0172, equivalently Bujokas-Patel: the Casnati-Ekedahl bundle of a general cover in H_{d,g} is balanced for g>=(d-3)(d-1), hence at (d,g)=(4,6)). The constant (CE)+(N)+(BAL) family over S with this fibre is an allowed ATT-0112 clause-(E) base: its classifying image is a single type-(i) point, hence not contained in the type-(ii) locus. For this family, U isomorphic to S times U_0 and Z isomorphic to S times Z_0, where U_0 is the reduced-support open in |L_0| isomorphic to P^2, a smooth connected surface, so H_c^4(U_0;Q)=Q(-2) of type (2,2). Compact-support Kunneth therefore realises Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S;Q)(-2) as a direct mixed-Hodge-structure summand of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(U;Q), carrying a nonzero Hodge type-(10,6) class (permitted by Deligne's Hodge-number bound on the 10-fold U). Finite-etale transfer over Q injects this S_6-invariant class into Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q). A finite direct sum of Q(-8) is pure of type (8,8), so Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(Z;Q) is not a finite direct sum of Q(-8) and T_16(Z):=W_{-16} H^{BM}_{16}(Z;Q), dual with no extra Tate twist, is not a finite direct sum of Q(8). Consequently the exact TASK-C66-M-004/C66-TATE-SUPPORT theorem, as universally quantified over every reduced locally Noetherian C-scheme carrying a (CE)+(N)+(BAL) genus-six degree-four family with no connected-component image contained in the type-(ii) locus and with no dimension, dominance, or non-isotriviality hypothesis, is false. The witness lies entirely in the simply-branched locus and already in the S_6-invariant ([6]) isotypic component. The class is a Kunneth summand of H_c^{16}(U) itself, namely the third FND-0167 corner Gr^W_12 H_c^{12}(S)(-2), not a lift of Gr^W_16 H_c^{16}(S), so FND-0171 does not block it. This does not resolve RED-0001, does not address T_16 of a dimension-17 model over a named 15-dimensional etale atlas of Hbar^bal, and does not refute the conditional implication of FND-0167, because the witness base violates (H-S) at j=6 and at j=7 (while the j=8 instance of (H-S) holds for this particular S).","numLines":10,"startLine":128,"totalLines":170}}}
