{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XzxdbkHexHho71bF2mtj93","type":"tool_result","content":"126	- `FND-0164` [corroborated; {'attempt_id': 'ATT-0113', 'case': {'g': 6, 'n': 6}, 'coefficients': 'Q', 'does_not_kill': 'Gr^W_{p+w} H_c^p(B;V)', 'failed_claim_id': 'CLM-0113-5', 'ground_field': 'algebraically closed of characteristic zero', 'hypotheses': ["V a constructible mixed Hodge module or admissible variation of mixed Hodge structure of weights at most w in Saito's convention", 'B separated of finite type over k', 'the constant-coefficient vanishing Gr^W_p H_c^p(B;Q)=0 is not assumed to transfer', 'exception when V is a constant mixed Hodge structure or constant Tate twist'], 'objects': ['H_c^p(B;R^q f_! Q)', 'compact-support Leray spectral sequence of mixed Hodge structures', 'Gr^W_{p+q}'], 'subproblem_id': 'C66-TATE-SUPPORT'}]: Let k be algebraically closed of characteristic zero. Let B be a separated finite-type k-scheme, and let V be a constructible mixed Hodge module on B, or an admissible variation of mixed Hodge structure viewed in D^b MHM(B), of weights at most w in Saito's convention (Gr_k^W H^i(V)=0 for all k>i+w). Compactly supported hypercohomology H_c^p(B;V) then has weights at most p+w, so the ceiling permits a possibly nonzero Gr^W_{p+w} rather than excluding it. Vanishing of Gr^W_p H_c^p(B;Q), including the vanishing obtained by compact-support localization of B as a dense open in a smooth affine d-fold when p<d, does not imply Gr^W_{p+w} H_c^p(B;V)=0 unless V is a constant mixed Hodge structure, in particular a constant Tate twist Q(-m). For a polarizable variation of Hodge structure of weight w, the lowest weight of ordinary H^p(B;V) is the image of intersection cohomology of the intermediate extension, pure of weight p+w; dually Gr^W_{p+w} H_c^p(B;V) is that top-weight piece and is not a functor of H_c^p(B;Q). A weight-w summand of V supported on a p-dimensional stratum likewise contributes in weight p+w. Consequently, in a compact-support Leray spectral sequence E_2^{p,q}=H_c^p(B; R^q f_! Q) of mixed Hodge structures, the estimate weights<=p+q does not kill Gr^W_{p+q}; additional control of the constructible coefficient object (constancy, lisseness, strata, or a weight-controlled extension across an affine ambient) or of the weight-(p+q) differentials is required. Exception: if R^q f_! Q is a constant Tate object, the identification H_c^p(B;Q(-m)) isomorphic to H_c^p(B;Q)(-m) does transfer the constant-coefficient top-weight vanishing. In the ATT-0113 setting this obstruction applies to the affine relative-dimension-2 morphism f:U->X^bal, with B=X^bal a dense open in a smooth affine 15-fold and with total degree p+q=16 for p<=14; the parenthetical alternative of running localization for a bounded complex of sheaves equally requires an unsupplied extension of R^q f_! Q across Y=X\X^bal, and dual Artin vanishing on the affine ambient does not apply to j_! of a local system from a proper open nor to general constructible sheaves.
